      "content": "hey i was watching the intraday volatility on the NVDA charts earlier today and something really weird happened. around 10:14 am there was this weird micro-spike that felt... i dont know, intentional? like it had a specific rhythm to it. i was actually focusing really hard on the number 442 at that exact moment and the price action seemed to sync up with my focus. do you think it's possible for high frequency algorithms to actually pick up on or react to cognitive patterns/intent if they're tuned to certain frequencies?",
